Z||000006||RobertVol||05-31-2001||01:21 AM||||They are using Vortech now? hmmm<P>I will be checking this out. I have been wanting to do this for awhile. hmm well,<P>Back to looking into this kit information <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>Robert<BR>88GT 56k T TOP  <BR>North Florida Fiero Club<P>CLICK BELOW AND SEE OUR SITE !!! <BR>NEXT MEETING - May 26th, in Jacksonville<BR><A HREF="http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros" TARGET=_blank>http://fullspeed.to/NorthFLFieros</A><BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/RobsGT2.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000007||grinthock||05-31-2001||07:22 AM||||I spoke with the FieroShop about that kit, they were also designing a kit (project on hold, not enough demand)  They ALSO used the Rotrex unit, what happened is, the Rotrex unit has been discontinued, so parts and the like are not available for it, can't get new ones to replace warrantied units, stuff like that. That's why they changed to the Vortec, the Vortec is also a better quality unit.<P>I remember the same post Slammed, he has said he got it, had some small install problems but RSM was able to help them, I also considered buying the kit from them...||||reg||1
Z||000008||grinthock||05-31-2001||07:26 AM||||One other note too, I remmeber that RaceTech/Fiero Shop put the same kit (modified mounting bracket) on a 3.1 Z24, they had to add a Fuel Press Reg and bigger injectors to get it running right, I know he added all sort of other stuff too, like MSD and various other toys||||reg||1
Z||000009||Greg Piet||05-31-2001||04:01 PM||||OK so here is where my questions arise.<BR>First I was thinking of 7-9 psi boost to begin and then go from there.<BR>I can completely understand that higher fuel pressure will be needed.<P>What injectors are "bigger" and where would they be acquired?<BR>What fuel pump do I NEED(will stock suffice)?<BR>I have a MSD, but not the Boost timing control unit so I guess that will be another item.<P>I will have the Fierostore Underdrive pulley, so would the reccomendation be going back to stock or just using a different SC pulley to get the desired boost?<P><BR>Sure I could just slap it tgether and slowly get all the quirks out of the system, but if someone has previous experience with this it would save me time and aggrivation.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000010||grinthock||05-31-2001||05:04 PM||||You are heading in a direction that may require alot of tweaking, dyno time and otherwise.  Do yourself a favor, at that PSI boost get a fuel pressure reg, it's worth it, to make sure the fuel is there for the project... As for injectors I have heard about people putting in 3.1 injectors as well as other various combinations.... Anyone else have a comment on that?  I am not a authority on the injector swaps.... The Turbo that a guy has here in town has the MSD Digital-6 with the retard and all that jazz... (also has the drag racing toys in it)||||reg||1
