Z||000012||grinthock||05-31-2001||05:33 PM||||RaceTech/FieroShop's unit was supposed to work WITH AC (different connector plate) but they never finished the development...||||reg||1
Z||000013||Sillhouette.com||06-01-2001||07:50 AM||||Hello !<P>Yep we do have the Vortech unit for the stock 2.8 fiero.  Do you have a 2.8 stroked to 3.1 or is it a 3.1 DIS engine from another car.  The reason I ask is the computer has to be programmed accordingly.  The 2.8 computer gets reprogrammed with the current system.  You don't need anything extra MSD or bigger injectors.  It works fine with the stock unit.  (for 7-10 psi)  If you want to go more drastic like 20PSI than you also need to think about lower compression pistons.  The Vortech unit is able to put 20 psi into the engine so the pressure depends on the size of the pulley. <P>The racetech supercharger would not work because of installation issues.  They wanted to put the supercharger by the Battery an run it backwards but the design of the bracket would be so complex that four V8 installs would not compare in price.  Next the supercharger was mounted to the chasi while the engine moved so now you have belt tensioning issues.  I know about this because five years ago that was the plan I had to install the the supercharger into the Fiero.  This was when racetch and RSM were one.  We found that it's financially and practically impossible so we gave up on that.  <P>The Vortech system gives a lot of torque.  More as a matter of fact than horsepower.  It was designed for track use I'm confident it will brake the 13s mark on the track.  I'll post the times when I get to the track.  <P>Later. ||||reg||1
Z||000014||Mr.Frosty||06-01-2001||11:25 AM||||Hey Sillhouette.com,<BR>  Do you reprogram the 2.8 ECM's.If so could you give everyone a price? Can you reprogram one for a Turbo App.?<P>------------------<BR>85 GT Turbo intercooled||||reg||1
Z||000015||p4n1c||06-01-2001||11:36 AM||||Can this be used for the 2.8 DIS engine?  Like for my car('88 Cutlass/S International).<P>Thanks<P>------------------<BR>-=-=-=[ p4n1c ]=-=-=-<BR>1988 Olds Cutlass Supreme International<BR>2.8L MPFI V6/TH440-T4 OD auto<BR>"Ride the geriatric mobile.. err..  rocket"||||reg||1
Z||000016||Greg Piet||06-01-2001||12:06 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Sillhouette.com:<BR><B>Hello !<P>Yep we do have the Vortech unit for the stock 2.8 fiero.  Do you have a 2.8 stroked to 3.1 or is it a 3.1 DIS engine from another car.  </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I have a 1985 block stroked with the 3.1 kit from ARI Racing engines.<P>Those  Boost values are right in my ballpark,  but I guess you are the person to ask about my pulley question.<BR>I have that underdrive pulley from the Fiero Store (24% smaller).   So do I need to go back to stock, or use a different pulley on the SC to get the desired boost.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000017||BV MotorSports||06-01-2001||04:17 PM||||Make sure you get a rising rate fuel pressure regulator or boost referenced fuel pressure regulator. Good safety item. A good A/F guage will also let you know whats going on inside your engine b4 you hear the expensive sounds!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>For over 6-8 pounds of boost an intercooler is highly recomended! Yes, even in supercharged form you will heat up the air/fuel mixture. s/c like paxton, vortech etc are alot like a turbo in that they operate at a higher rpm that say a roots/eaton s/c (like the GM 3.8v6).<BR>An i/c from a daytona turbo is small and very eficient for its size. U can pick these up for under $50 at a j-yard. If you dont have the "ram-air" scoops think of getting them so you could mount your i/c inside of one and maybe a oil cooler. Usually dont need an oil cooler unless or temp reaches 260deg or higher at ANY TIME.<P>Good luck.<P>Steven<P>------------------<BR>87 Fiero GT 14.9/ 93mph<BR>94 Formula WS6 w/ NOS 12.4 /118mph<BR>87 Conquest TSi <BR>85.5 Starion ESi||||reg||4
Z||000018||Sillhouette.com||06-01-2001||04:44 PM||||Here are some answers!<P>I can reprogram the 2.8 PROM for the turbo application.  How much boost are you running what type of turbo, engine and so on.  The most efficient way would be to drop the engine off at RSM and let me at it for a couple of days.  Failing that we have to play tag with your computer until we get it just right.  Meaning you'll send your ECM I'll reprogram it send it back to you than you test it if you find bugs send it back I'll adjust it some more and so on.  It sounds long but it's do-able. For price it's $200 canadian for the work.  On top of this there is the corcharge if you don't supply the ECM with a Prom and shipping<P>For supercharging the 2.8DIS engine I would probably use the 3.1 turbo Mclaren ECM and reprogram it from there.  I have not put a lot of thought into it.  If you're interested let me know and I'll research it further.  <P>Calculating the boost values for the G90 Vortech.  It is a V9 Trim supercharger so go to this site to calculate the impeller speed. <A HREF="http://www.vortechsupercharger.com/tech/impspeed.html" TARGET=_blank>www.vortechsupercharger.com/tech/impspeed.html</A>   <BR>The G90 puts out 20psi max at 62000 rpm impeller speed.  For 10 psi you want to run it 31000 rpm.  Now adjust the supercharger pulley to get the desired impeller speed.  Keep in mind that there is about 1-2psi of parasitic loss.  So a 10 psi system will run only 8 psi in real life.<P>Later||||reg||1
